   "complete": true,
   "final_text": "`kvconf get app.conf app.title` now prints `Issue #42: retry`. `go test ./...` passes, and `checks/quoted-hash.sh` reports ok.\n\nThe fix is in `parseValue` in `parser.go`. An unquoted value still ends at the first `#`. A value that starts with `\"` is now read character by character up to the closing quote. `\\\"` and `\\\\` are unescaped along the way. After the closing quote, only whitespace or a `# ...` comment is allowed.\n\nI added `TestQuotedHash` to `parser_test.go`. It covers the quoted `#`, `\"x\" # note`, `\"C:\\\\temp\"`, and a value that has an escaped quote and a `#` inside quotes followed by a trailing comment. The existing `TestValues` already checks `port = 8080 # http`.\n\nOne behaviour change: text after the closing quote that isn't a comment, such as `\"x\" y`, now gives the error `unexpected text after quoted value`. Before, it gave `unterminated quoted value`.\n\nSTATUS: DONE",
